vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper: FinishEveryRender, to skip the glFinish of an untimed render

vtkOpenGLGPUVolumeRayCastMapper::GPURender ends every render with glFinish(),
so that the timer in vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper::Render measures the GPU's
work. That time is used in one place: with AutoAdjustSampleDistances on, it
chooses the next render's image sample distance. (It also becomes the volume's
EstimatedRenderTime, in vtkVolume::RenderVolumetricGeometry.)

Every other render pays for the wait too. The CPU stops until the GPU has run
everything queued so far (the scene's opaque geometry, then the ray cast), and
the GPU then idles while the CPU prepares the rest of the frame and the next:
the two times add up instead of overlapping. In an application that renders
continuously (libcvc's terrain_lab: a terrain, water and its nearest clouds as
GPU ray-cast volumes, 1280x720 on an Intel Arc iGPU, Windows), the wait was
45-48 % of the main thread's samples, about 25 ms of a 45 ms frame. Without it
the frame took 18 ms, and the images were byte-identical.

This adds vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper::FinishEveryRender. On, the default,
nothing changes. Off, a render waits only when AutoAdjustSampleDistances is on,
the one case that uses its time; any other render returns once its work is
queued, and its TimeToDraw is the CPU's part only.

vtkSmartVolumeMapper gets the same property and forwards it to the GPU mapper
it renders with, beside the AutoAdjustSampleDistances it already sets per
render from the render window's desired update rate. So with FinishEveryRender
off, an interactive render (a drag) still waits and adjusts its quality as
before, and a still render does not wait.

It is opt-in because TimeToDraw and EstimatedRenderTime change meaning when it
is off, and code outside the mapper (vtkLODProp3D, an application's own time
budget) may rely on them measuring the GPU.

--- a/Rendering/Volume/vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper.h
+++ b/Rendering/Volume/vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper.h
@@ -49,6 +49,28 @@
 
   ///@{
   /**
+   * If FinishEveryRender is on, every render waits for the GPU to finish its
+   * work (glFinish in the OpenGL implementation) before it returns, so that
+   * the time it takes (TimeToDraw, and the volume's EstimatedRenderTime with
+   * it) measures the GPU's work.
+   *
+   * If it is off, only a render with AutoAdjustSampleDistances on waits, since
+   * only that render uses its own time (to choose the next render's image
+   * sample distance). Any other render returns as soon as its work is queued,
+   * so the GPU can ray cast while the CPU prepares the rest of the frame, and
+   * its TimeToDraw is the CPU's part only. Turn it off when nothing needs the
+   * draw time of a still render: an application that renders continuously and
+   * paces its own frames, say.
+   *
+   * On by default.
+   */
+  vtkSetMacro(FinishEveryRender, vtkTypeBool);
+  vtkGetMacro(FinishEveryRender, vtkTypeBool);
+  vtkBooleanMacro(FinishEveryRender, vtkTypeBool);
+  ///@}
+
+  ///@{
+  /**
    * Compute the sample distance from the data spacing.  When the number of
    * voxels is 8, the sample distance will be roughly 1/200 the average voxel
    * size. The distance will grow proportionally to numVoxels^(1/3). Off by default.
@@ -521,6 +543,7 @@
 
   vtkTypeBool LockSampleDistanceToInputSpacing;
   vtkTypeBool AutoAdjustSampleDistances;
+  vtkTypeBool FinishEveryRender;
   float ImageSampleDistance;
   float MinimumImageSampleDistance;
   float MaximumImageSampleDistance;
--- a/Rendering/Volume/vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper.cxx
+++ b/Rendering/Volume/vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper.cxx
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
   : LockSampleDistanceToInputSpacing(0)
 {
   this->AutoAdjustSampleDistances = 1;
+  this->FinishEveryRender = 1;
   this->ImageSampleDistance = 1.0;
   this->MinimumImageSampleDistance = 1.0;
   this->MaximumImageSampleDistance = 10.0;
@@ -594,6 +595,7 @@
   this->Superclass::PrintSelf(os, indent);
 
   os << indent << "AutoAdjustSampleDistances: " << this->AutoAdjustSampleDistances << endl;
+  os << indent << "FinishEveryRender: " << this->FinishEveryRender << endl;
   os << indent << "MinimumImageSampleDistance: " << this->MinimumImageSampleDistance << endl;
   os << indent << "MaximumImageSampleDistance: " << this->MaximumImageSampleDistance << endl;
   os << indent << "ImageSampleDistance: " << this->ImageSampleDistance << endl;
--- a/Rendering/VolumeOpenGL2/vtkOpenGLGPUVolumeRayCastMapper.cxx
+++ b/Rendering/VolumeOpenGL2/vtkOpenGLGPUVolumeRayCastMapper.cxx
@@ -3306,7 +3306,13 @@
     }
   }
 
-  glFinish();
+  // Wait for the GPU, so that the timer around this render (TimeToDraw) measures its work: always
+  // when FinishEveryRender is on, else only when this render's time chooses the next render's
+  // sample distance (AutoAdjustSampleDistances). Otherwise return with the work queued.
+  if (this->FinishEveryRender || this->AutoAdjustSampleDistances)
+  {
+    glFinish();
+  }
 
   // Restore the previous scattering blending settings
   this->VolumetricScatteringBlending = previousVolumetricScatteringBlending;
